OL,3,GNEWSAChief constable apologises after
OL,4,Aex-senior officer discriminated against
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe chief constable has apologised to a
OL,7,Fformer PSNI chief inspector for
OL,8,Fdiscrimination she suffered in the
OL,9,Fforce.
OL,11,FUrsula Merrick, who has been medically
OL,12,Fretired, was subjected to "unwarranted
OL,13,Fand highly damaging allegations" by her
OL,14,Fformer colleague, Supt Ian Campbell,
OL,15,Fwho is now retired.
OL,17,FIn 2023, an employment tribunal found
OL,18,Fthat Ch Insp Ursula Merrick was
OL,19,Fdiscriminated on grounds of her sex and
OL,20,Fdisability.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,414,410,260,120,0,100
